    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## When to use\nUse when creating, extending, or redesigning a Powerhouse document model \u2014 defining or changing its state schema, modules, operations, operation errors, or reducer implementations.\n\n## What it covers\n- Workflow\n- Common mistakes\n- DM.00.1 Ensure you have the required input and context\n- DM.00.2 Confirm the reactor is running and reachable\n- DM.00.3 Review the existing package specs and implementation\n- DM.00.4 Ensure the Reactor Package information is sufficiently updated\n- Expected Scenario Outcome\n- DM.01.1 Ensure the document model specification document exists in Vetra Drive\n- DM.01.2 Start by listing the users who will use the new document model\n- DM.01.3 Come up with a good, concise description\n- DM.01.4 Fill out the remaining header fields\n- DM.02.1 Define the global state schema\n- DM.02.2 Generate a minimal default value for the document\n- DM.02.3 Define the modules and operations titles\n\n## Where the full skill lives\n- Vault source: **Agent skill: document-modeling** (full text, DERIVED_FROM below) \u2014 the vault is this skill's home.\n- Upstream origin: https://github.com/powerhouse-inc/powerhouse-dev-skills/tree/main/skills/document-modeling\n\n## Invocation\nRead the vault source content and follow it. Not a plugin command.\n\n_Added via add-skill; content hash sha256:9f87f3e783bb\u2026_",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-17T12:10:57.493Z"
